WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
[Inaudible babble]

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.160
90 minutes before the vice presidential debate even got started,

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.799
the GOP mistakenly tweeted and posted an article saying that

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:16.619
Mike Pence had clearly won.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.600
That tells you everything you need to know about tonight's debate

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.020
and you didn't need to watch it.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.400
What we need more than ever in American politics

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.180
are not politicians that simply talk over each other

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.880
and trod out scripted one-liners

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.020
that would have been tired in a 90s sitcom.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.760
Do you want a "you're hired" president in Hillary Clinton

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.160
or a "you're fired" president in Donald Trump?

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.660
[Applause]

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.180
We need different points of view

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.520
and we need more voices on the stage.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.640
And if we don't get that,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.640
it's not going to get any better than this:

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:45.930
You whipped out that Mexican thing again.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:52.080
For Reason TV, I'm Nick Gillespie.

